For a fixed $k$, we need to calculate the weights of the $n/k$ trucks.
Let $P$ be the prefix sum array of $a$, where $P_0 = 0$ and $P_i = \sum_{j=1}^i a_j$.
The weight of the $j$-th truck (where $1 \le j \le n/k$) is $P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k}$.
We need to find $\max_{j} (P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k}) - \min_{j} (P_{jk} - P_{(j-1)k})$.

Let's analyze the complexity.
If we iterate over all divisors $k$ of $n$, for each $k$, we iterate through the trucks. There are $n/k$ trucks.
The total complexity would be $\sum_{k|n} \frac{n}{k} = \sum_{d|n} d$.
